WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:06.280
This idea sounds like science fiction, but by&nbsp;
the end of the video, you will see that this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:14.640
makes perfect sense. So, what is it? Well,&nbsp;
consider image inpainting. It is amazing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:22.160
What can it do? Well, when we cut out a part&nbsp;
of an image, then, bam! It fills in the void&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:29.720
with plausible information. This is image&nbsp;
inpainting. And now it works on video too.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:38.160
But it gets even crazier. Image outpainting&nbsp;
also works. Whoa! What is that? Well, we can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:46.400
essentially extend the image in any direction&nbsp;
and once again, fill it in with plausible data.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:53.960
Now please note the choice of words here: in&nbsp;
both cases I said it fills it in with plausible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.960 --> 00:01:02.320
data. Data that could be there. But synthetic&nbsp;
data nonetheless. Now here is an insane idea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:09.120
from Google’s researchers. What if we would take&nbsp;
these, and fill them in in not with information&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:17.440
that could have been there, but with information&nbsp;
that was actually there. Filling in with reality.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:25.680
That is of course, impossible, right? Well,&nbsp;
look. Oh yes. It seems like it is impossible.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:31.720
If we try to complete this image with previous&nbsp;
techniques, for instance, Stable Diffusion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:38.920
we get something that is plausible, you know,&nbsp;
the hat continues, the post its also continue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:46.240
that is good, but still it is likely not the&nbsp;
real thing. So, can I get the real thing?

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:54.040
Well, let’s think together. What if we are trying&nbsp;
to outpaint a historical building? Wait a minute,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:59.840
that is the key! If we try to fill in information&nbsp;
for something that we have other photos for,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:06.240
it might be possible. Let’s give it a&nbsp;
try. This is the incomplete input photo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:14.360
and here are our other photos. Now note that this&nbsp;
is still quite hard. We can’t just copy it. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:21.200
angles are different, the lighting is different,&nbsp;
lens distortion is really different. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:30.200
in the age of AI, let’s see if it can be&nbsp;
done. And…oh wow! Look at that! Perfection.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:36.160
And it can do it for a variety of scenes&nbsp;
over and over again. It appears to work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:40.080
pretty much everywhere. Well,&nbsp;
it does not work everywhere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:45.840
I’ll tell you about it in a moment.&nbsp;
But, all this is absolutely amazing.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:52.560
But still, wait. How do we know how real these&nbsp;
photos are if there is nothing to compare to?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.560 --> 00:03:00.040
Well, let’s make sure that there is something to&nbsp;
compare to. Let’s take a real photo, cut off the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:07.800
top, and now we know exactly what should be there.&nbsp;
Stable Diffusion does not know. Paint by Example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:14.040
a paper from almost exactly a year ago&nbsp;
does not know at all. But the new technique&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:23.160
called RealFill, this one knows. Look. That is&nbsp;
incredible. Almost pixel perfect reconstruction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:29.200
My goodness. What a time to be alive! Now&nbsp;
note that this is not a copying machine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:35.960
it has access to information about the room,&nbsp;
but it has to understand which part is missing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:41.920
and what that part would look like from&nbsp;
this angle. So it fills in reality after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:47.400
all. And it does it over and over&nbsp;
again with breathtaking accuracy.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:51.440
Now, I noted that it is still not perfect. I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:56.920
all of these look nearly&nbsp;
perfect. So where are the issues?

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:04.640
Ah. Of course. Text. It’s always the text.&nbsp;
Every time. We finally left behind the age&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:12.840
of AI systems generating mangled, incorrect&nbsp;
hands, mostly, but text is still a challenge.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:19.600
I am fairly sure that this is something that will&nbsp;
be possible just one more paper down the line.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:26.640
And can you imagine what will be possible two&nbsp;
more papers down the line? My goodness. We can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:36.280
already do a pretty good reconstruction from just&nbsp;
one image. Not even a set of images. One image.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:43.400
This is supposed to be a failure case. If this&nbsp;
is a failure case, bravo, sign me up right now!

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:50.240
So, adding a little more information to the&nbsp;
AI by reusing already existing images. That&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:56.600
was the crazy idea, which in hindsight,&nbsp;
makes perfect sense. What a brilliant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.600 --> 00:05:03.520
paper. Loving it! And one more thing. I have&nbsp;
a little daughter and when she was a baby,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:08.920
we could not really afford a good smartphone&nbsp;
to take better images of her. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:15.760
there are a lot of pictures, and I was thinking&nbsp;
that over my lifetime, there will surely be an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:22.320
AI that will be able to upscale those not great&nbsp;
images to a higher resolution version. And it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:30.440
should not just fill in things that could be, but&nbsp;
with things that are really there. And finally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:38.080
we are here. I can’t believe it. And all it&nbsp;
needs is one to three photos. And as a family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:43.240
we have thousands of photos of&nbsp;
ourselves to learn from. So good.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:06:00.880
